# Deny by default.
#
# The working data in this repo is real ticket content - the work store holds
# material subject to company rules, the other holds personal work.
# So nothing is tracked unless it is opted in below. The important consequence:
# a store added later is ignored automatically, rather than needing its name
# added here. dashboard.py treats any folder containing a tickets/ subfolder as
# a store and needs no code change to gain one, so an ignore list written by
# name would silently fail to cover the next one.
*

# Descend into directories so the rules below can match inside them. Without
# this, git never looks inside a folder and the un-ignore rules never fire.
!*/

# --- tracked ---------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENSE is named explicitly: it has no extension, so the *.md and *.py rules
# below would not have caught it and it would have been left out of the repo.
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!*.py
!*.md
!docs/example-ticket.json

# ...except the original handover note, which stays local. It was written as a
# private working document, and its useful conclusions have since been folded
# into CLAUDE.md anyway.
docs/HANDOVER-ARCHIVE.md

# --- never tracked, even if a rule above widens ----------------------------
# .tmp/ is a store's scratch space for in-progress writes. .ids/ is its record
# of every ticket ID ever issued. Both are per-store working state that belongs
# with the data, not the code, and the data is not tracked. Listed as
# directories so git never descends into them, rather than relying on the
# deny-by-default rule to catch each file inside.
# .ticket-scope is a per-machine marker saying which store this folder uses.
.tmp/
.ids/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ticket-scope
